@startuml agent_cancellation_evidence
' Java baseline: 58dd747a; implementation: 8bed9b10.
' Source: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java#runInternal,#runTurns.
' Source: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java#execute,#applyBeforeHook.
' Source: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/event/AgentEndEvent.java.
' Pi baseline: 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3.
' Pi source: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts#runLoop,#prepareToolCall.
' Observed behavior: Java can exit tool cancellation without another Assistant ABORTED message.
' Java divergence: supplement agent_end with cancellation evidence; do not append a cancelled hook result.
' Design reason: preserve natural completion when a cancellation request arrives late.
title Agent cancellation evidence
start
:Run model and tool turns;
if (Natural end returned?) then (yes)
  :cancelled = false;
else (no)
  if (Token caused loop exit or cancellation?) then (yes)
    :cancelled = true;
  else (no)
    :Propagate failure;
    :cancelled = false;
  endif
endif
:Emit AgentEnd in finally;
note right
  Assistant ABORTED and actual exceptions
  remain separate outcome evidence.
  A false flag does not prove success.
end note
stop
@enduml
